<title>FINLAND: Finnish Jan trade surplus FIM 4.0 billion - customs.</title>
<headline>Finnish Jan trade surplus FIM 4.0 billion - customs.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's trade surplus rose to 4.0 billion markka in January from 1.9 billion in December and from 2.8 billion in January last year, the National Customs Board (NCB) said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The value of exports rose 13 percent year-on-year in January while the value of imports rose five percent, NCB said.  </p>
<p>Preliminary trade balance (million markka):</p>
<p>		  Jan '97    Dec '96    Jan '96</p>
<p> Exports	 15,000     14,619     13,325</p>
<p> Imports	 11,000     12,764     10,526</p>
<p> Balance	 +4,000     +1,855     +2,799</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
